# A zero-length WinZip AES entry still carries an authentication code (HMAC).
# Here the 10-byte HMAC of an empty AES-256 entry is corrupted; reading it with
# the correct password must fail instead of returning the entry as a valid empty
# file.
features HAVE_CRYPTO
return 1
arguments empty-badmac-aes256.zzip
stdin
set_default_password password
cat -i 0
end-of-inline-data
file empty-badmac-aes256.zzip empty-badmac-aes256.zip
stderr
*stdin*:2: cat: can't read file at index 0: CRC error
end-of-inline-data
